{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Be ready for three days.</b> At the end of three days — that is the fourth day. Moses added one day on his own, according to the words of Rabbi Yosei; but according to the one who says the Ten Commandments were given on the sixth of the month, Moses added nothing at all, and 'for three days' means 'for the third day.'" "<b>Do not approach a woman.</b> All these three days — so that the women would immerse on the third day and be pure to receive the Torah. For if they had relations within three days, perhaps the woman would emit semen after her immersion and become impure again; but once three days have passed, the semen has putrefied and is no longer fit to fertilize, and is pure from impurifying the one who emits it (Shabbat 86a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:07.545569184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}